#: includes/dashboard.php:455
msgid "Which files can I use?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/dashboard.php:455
msgid "GLB (one file, recommended) and glTF. Keep them small for fast pages, ideally under 5 MB. For iPhone and iPad, the viewer turns the GLB into the format AR needs by itself."
msgstr ""

#: includes/dashboard.php:456
msgid "How do hotspots work?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/dashboard.php:456
msgid "In the block, open Hotspots on the General tab; on a product, use the preview in its 3D model tab. Click \"Add hotspot\", then click on the model where it goes, and give it a label and an optional text. The point turns with the model and fades when it is behind it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/dashboard.php:457
msgid "Why is there no \"View in your room\" button on my computer?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/dashboard.php:457
msgid "Augmented reality needs a phone or tablet with a camera and AR support. On other devices the button stays hidden, and visitors can still turn and zoom the model."
msgstr ""

#: includes/dashboard.php:458
msgid "Where is the View in 3D button on my product?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/dashboard.php:458
msgid "It shows under the product images once the product has a model in its 3D model tab. Block themes get it below the product image gallery block, classic themes like Storefront below the gallery."
msgstr ""

#: includes/dashboard.php:459
msgid "Does the plugin collect any data?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/dashboard.php:459
msgid "Nothing from your visitors. From you, only if you click \"Allow & Continue\" on the opt-in: your name and email, your site address, title and language, and the WordPress, PHP and plugin versions, through Freemius. You can opt out from the Plugins page at any time."
msgstr ""

